---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Container from '../components/layout/Container.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

const updated = 'August 2026';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="Privacy at Webcam Test: your camera and microphone feeds are processed entirely in your browser and are never uploaded or transmitted."
>
  <Container class="py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
      <p class="caption-mono uppercase text-mute">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="display-xl mt-3 text-ink">Your feed stays on your device.</h1>
      <p class="body-lg mt-6 text-body">
        {SITE.name} is built so that your camera and microphone data never leaves your computer
        or phone. This page explains exactly what happens, in plain language and without the
        usual hedging.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas-soft p-6">
        <p class="caption-mono uppercase text-mute">The short version</p>
        <ul class="body-md mt-4 list-disc space-y-2 ps-5 text-body">
          <li>Your video and audio are processed in your browser and are never uploaded.</li>
          <li>We do not operate a server that receives media, so we could not see it if we tried.</li>
          <li>No account, no email address, and no personal details are ever requested.</li>
          <li>Snapshots and recorded clips are created locally and stay on your device.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-12 text-ink">Camera and microphone</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        When you start a test, your browser asks for permission and then hands the media stream
        directly to the page. The preview you see and every measurement we report resolution,
        frame rate, aspect ratio, audio level, are computed in your browser on frames that
        exist only in your device’s memory. Nothing is uploaded, recorded, stored, or
        transmitted, and this site is a set of static files with no media endpoint to receive
        such data.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Snapshots</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        If you capture a snapshot, the image is drawn from the live video in your browser and
        downloaded straight to your device. It is never sent anywhere, and we retain no copy.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Recordings</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        The optional “see what others see” clip is recorded by your browser into memory on
        your own device and played back from there. It is not uploaded, and it is discarded
        as soon as you press Discard, start another recording, stop the test, or close the
        tab. It is only ever written to disk if you choose Download.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Permissions</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        Access lasts only while you are testing. Pressing “Stop”, closing the tab, or navigating
        away releases the camera and microphone immediately, your camera indicator light turns
        off, which is your own independent confirmation. You can withdraw permission at any time
        from your browser’s site settings, described in our{' '}
        <a class="text-link hover:text-link-deep" href="/troubleshooting#permissions">permissions guide</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">What we store in your browser</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        One item: your light or dark theme choice, saved in your browser’s local storage so the
        site does not flash the wrong colours on your next visit. It stays on your device, is
        not a tracking identifier, and is removed when you clear site data. We do not use
        advertising or tracking cookies.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Analytics</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        We may collect anonymous, aggregate statistics about the website itself page views and
        which tools are used, to understand what to improve. This never includes your camera or
        microphone content, and it is never used to build a profile of you.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Children</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        This site is a general-purpose utility and is not directed at children. Because we do not
        collect personal information from anyone, we hold no personal information about children.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        If this policy changes, the revised version will be posted on this page with a new date
        below. Any change that affects how your data is handled will be described in plain terms
        rather than buried in a revision.
      </p>

      <h2 class="display-md mt-10 text-ink">Contact</h2>
      <p class="body-md mt-4 text-body">
        Questions about privacy can be sent to{' '}
        <a class="text-link hover:text-link-deep" href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
      </p>

      <p class="caption mt-12 text-mute">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </Container>
</Layout>
